WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.860
Misses, neither of you will ever be returning to Souai Middle School again.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.030
Oh stop it, Kenmochi-san.
What are you talking about?

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:45.610
The master contacted me and you’re to be transferred back to your old middle school.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.830
The arrangements are
to be made immediately.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.590
This is all for your sake, Misses.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.120
Transfer?

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:04.470
Finally, the entrance exams will begin.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:09.480
Be prepared for anything, and do your best to clear this last hurdle.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:14.390
Most importantly, make sure you get enough sleep.

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.200
Mind you, this does not mean sleeping in class or on the train.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:25.250
Even though it’s February, Kira-chan and Yura-chan remain absent from school.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:30.830
A whole month has passed since the Sakurazuki sisters stopped coming to class.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:33.050
That’s why I gave them a call.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.660
You did?

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.990
How are the Sakurazuki sisters?

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:41.860
The butler said that the ladies would not be coming to the phone.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:46.180
It was the same for me.
It won’t work even if a girl calls?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:50.550
Really? I wonder what the
Sakurazuki sisters are doing.

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:54.580
Futami-kun, you should be well-informed. Don’t you know anything about it?

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.280
Um, nope. Nothing at all.

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.130
I see.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.940
It makes you worry, doesn’t it?

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:03.420
No matter how you look at it, these absences are just too frequent.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.240
I know that the girls are worrying about you, Futami-san.

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:10.610
Futami-san, please explain to them clearly how you feel.

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:16.780
Perhaps because I wasn’t frank with them, Kira-chan and Yura-chan felt hurt…

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.760
So much that they didn’t want to come to school…

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.550
Anyway, what is happening with them?

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.780
We can’t talk to them on the phone.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:28.110
Ai-sensei couldn’t meet with them either, right, Nozomu?

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.860
Hey, Nozomu!

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.610
Sorry, I was zoning out.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:37.940
Is this the time to space out?
February means Valentine’s Day!

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:44.150
Even if it’s out of obligation, I want chocolates from the Sakurazuki sisters.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:47.800
It’d probably be something very extravagant, like covered with gold dust.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.040
And because they’re twins, you get not one, but two!

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.660
You’re worried about chocolates? You sure are easy-going.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:59.170
It’s not easy. I’m really worried about the Sakurazuki sisters.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.450
I suppose.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:03.010
Nozomu-chan!

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.390
Nozomu-chan!

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:06.220
Oh, the Ichijou sisters.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:11.800
Say, I’m counting on you two for Valentine’s chocolates.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:15.770
Just out of obligation is fine, okay. Please? Please? PLEASE?!

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.020
We understand…

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.430
All right!

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:22.530
I knew you were easy-going.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:25.740
Nozomu-chan, about the Sakurazuki sisters…

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.540
Yes, they were absent today as well.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.540
I see, I wonder what really
happened to them.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.000
Yeah.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.300
Please, Kenmochi-san.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.820
We want to go to school,
no matter what.

00:04:42.820 --> 00:04:46.610
We’re tired of staying in the house all the time.

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:47.430
Please!

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.850
No matter how many times you ask, my decision will not change.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:57.430
The master will return from London next week.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.980
Following that, we will finalise the paperwork

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:03.110
…for your return to your
old middle school.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.240
We can’t go back to our old school!

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.530
It has to be Souai Middle School!

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:10.040
Kira-chan…

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.040
That would be impossible.

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:15.040
Kenmochi-san!

00:05:15.690 --> 00:05:21.090
To protect you ladies,
I would even become an ogre.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:36.550
It was no good today either,
and February means Valentine’s too…

00:05:36.550 --> 00:05:40.610
It’s the first important day since we fell in love with Nozomu-kun.

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:46.040
Yura-chan, let’s borrow the kitchen and make some chocolates now.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.860
For Papa and Kenmochi-san?

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:51.370
We’ll make some for them too, but really for Nozomu-kun…

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:52.870
Eh?

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.150
This will be our first
homemade chocolate.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:58.620
Even if we make it,
we can’t give it to him.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:01.800
We saw this movie on television earlier, right?

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:02.700
Movie?

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:06.120
The story where the princess snuck secretly into Rome.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.140
Oh yes.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:12.490
On Valentine’s, we could just sneak out
like the princess in that story.

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:15.850
Ah, but I would feel bad
for Kenmochi-san.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:22.460
Yura-chan, I know how much Kenmochi-san treasures us,

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:28.990
and I don’t want to sadden him too.
But… but this is the limit.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:34.370
Never to return to that school again, never to see Nozomu-kun again… I can’t take that!

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:36.410
Kira-chan…

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:41.030
It’ll be all right. If the two of us combine our strengths, we should be able to escape.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.090
Okay?

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:44.790
Yes.

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:47.010
That’s great!

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.330
We have to buy a lot of
ingredients this year.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.080
Father’s share last year was just fine,

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:07.870
but Kosaka-kun has come begging us for some, too.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:09.950
Of course we’ll get some for Nozomu-chan.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.580
Kaoruko.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.660
I…

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:25.500
I was thinking that I’d gather my courage and confess to Nozomu-chan on Valentine’s Day.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:34.040
B-but Sumireko, you said earlier that you wouldn’t confess.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:37.510
You said the way it is now – spending every day happily with everyone – is better…

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.120
I am very worried…

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:42.520
About the Sakurazuki sisters.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.330
He was with the Sakurazuki sisters at Hatsumode.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.330
Hatsumode: temple visit for the New Year

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:50.290
Probably on Christmas as well.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:55.120
Since the Sakurazuki sisters stopped coming to school, he has been very depressed.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:56.540
That’s right, isn’t it?

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:58.880
Even from our standpoint,

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:02.550
the Sakurazuki sisters seem like very honest and good girls, right?

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:03.540
Yes.

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:07.140
If I don’t confess now,

00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:11.190
I feel like Kira-chan and Yura-chan will steal Nozomu-chan away from us.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:17.270
And then, he’ll always think of me as a childhood friend.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.490
Sumireko…

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.820
That’s why… That’s why I must say it to Nozomu-chan.

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.250
Oh, I’m sorry. I got carried away.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:31.460
No problem. I understand your feelings, Sumireko.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:32.450
Really?

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:32.990
Yes.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:36.990
Say, Kaoruko…
Will you support me in this?

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.500
Yes, I will support you.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.510
Thank you.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.380
Nozomu-chan likes nuts in his chocolate, right?

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:51.880
I wonder if it’s strange to put almonds and cashews in together.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.880
It’s too late to say my feelings now.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:01.400
I could never say something like, “I love you too, Nozomu-chan.”

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:08.020
It was great when we were children.

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:12.210
That’s okay! We’ll both be your brides!

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:16.280
Of course! We’ll both be your wives, Nozomu-chan.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:20.410
Feeling that I loved him, I could honestly say it.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:23.870
Say, Kaoruko… Huh?

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:34.670
Kaoruko?

00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:39.330
The chocolate has melted.

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:41.650
Rara-chan, hold down the chocolate bowl firmly.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:43.640
Ruru-chan, stir it well.

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.760
Not like how you’d knead it into a cookie. Mix it just like that.

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:48.550
Yes.

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:50.280
Do your best, Ruru-chan.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.100
Onii-chan, look forward to this, okay?

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:55.740
The love chocolate of Rara and Ruru!

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:57.280
Ah, okay.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:05.290
All girls try so hard to make chocolate like that.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:09.920
Perhaps even Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan…

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:16.540
But now, Kaoruko-chan… she’s giving chocolate to Yuuya-kun.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.140
What am I thinking about?

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:22.680
I have the pure Kira-chan and Yura-chan,

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.140
whom I’ve saddened with my ambiguous attitude.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:29.110
Why am I so worried about
Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan?

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:32.240
I don’t know…

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.230
I don’t understand myself.

00:10:39.670 --> 00:10:42.220
Please allow us to help as well.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:44.330
It’s all right;
just leave us alone for now.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.080
But Misses…

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.470
No means no.

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:50.480
It has to be something that we make ourselves.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:56.380
It’ll be nice if we can
convey our feelings.

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:59.380
They will get across, I’m sure.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:12.650
Kaoruko.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:16.020
Kaoruko, what will you do?

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.030
Eh?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.990
Won’t you give some to Nozomu-chan? Chocolate.

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.630
I suppose, since I am his friend.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:24.910
Is that okay?

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:26.830
Are you really okay with that?

00:11:27.280 --> 00:11:28.830
What are you talking about,
all of a sudden?

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:34.130
Actually… don’t you love
Nozomu-chan too, Kaoruko?

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:39.010
I knew it was like that!

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:40.720
Sumireko…

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:42.960
I knew it was!

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.600
Why? Why didn’t you say anything?

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.880
Why did you say you would support me?

00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:49.770
That’s cruel! That’s too cruel, Kaoruko!

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.390
Why?

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:59.530
Why didn’t you say anything?

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.860
Why did you say you would support me?

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:03.450
That’s cruel! That’s too cruel, Kaoruko!

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:06.190
I just…

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.210
Sympathy?

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:12.840
Even if we’re twins, I always seemed to be your extra.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:14.750
Were you sympathizing over that?

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.780
An extra? What are you saying?

00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:21.660
Even now, he speaks of
“Kaoruko-chan and company.”

00:12:21.660 --> 00:12:23.720
He wouldn’t say
“Sumireko-chan and company.”

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:24.930
It’s not…

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.180
It was like that even
when we were children!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.390
Like I was just your add-on:

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:33.230
I would always be left behind, and I had to struggle just to keep up with you.

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.310
I was so jealous of you that I couldn’t stand it!

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:40.570
It’s true. I was always jealous of you, Kaoruko.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:46.180
You could always say what I couldn’t.
You could always do what I couldn’t.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.950
Kaoruko, you… you would never understand those feelings, would you, Kaoruko?!

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.370
Don’t be so one-sided!

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:53.370
One-sided?

00:12:53.760 --> 00:12:57.960
I was always jealous of you too, Sumireko!

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:04.290
As a child, you were always so calm, and you always thought things out well.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:09.830
Mama and Papa always told me to be more like you, Sumireko!

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:16.090
Even Nozomu-chan could count on you during crucial moments.

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:19.770
I always believed that there was no way I could compete with you, Sumireko.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:21.070
I was jealous of you, Sumireko!

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:22.440
It can’t be.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.770
Even this time with Nozomu-chan, it’s the same.

00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:28.030
Sumireko, if you said that
you loved him,

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.660
he would definitely think more deeply about it than if I said it.

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:36.040
On thinking that, there was no way
I could say it. To say that I love him…

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:42.050
Sumireko, do you understand my feelings? You don’t understand, do you?

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:45.050
Kaoruko.

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:05.030
It’s the same as the Grave of the Twins legend.

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:10.880
They fell in love with the same person, and that caused their suffering.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:16.720
I wonder why we fell in love with Nozomu-chan.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:21.380
The same feelings… two people have fallen in love with someone.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:23.890
The feelings trap them between a rock and a hard place.

00:14:23.890 --> 00:14:30.800
It’s so painful and sad, the twins became birds and flew away.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:35.240
If we became birds, that would be a lot easier, wouldn’t it?

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:36.940
That’s no good.

00:14:38.750 --> 00:14:41.270
That’s just no good, becoming birds.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:47.840
Because being in love with someone is supposed to be a happy thing, right?

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.910
It’s supposed to be something amazing, isn’t it?

00:14:50.510 --> 00:14:55.240
To put those feelings aside and run away – that’s just wrong!

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:57.510
Sumireko…

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:03.680
That’s true. You want to treasure these, right?

00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:06.760
These feelings of being in love with Nozomu-chan.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:12.060
So, Kaoruko, you will make him a chocolate of true love.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:16.770
Don’t hesitate on my account, and be more honest.

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:21.770
And I won’t hold back for you either, Kaoruko, I’ll be more honest.

00:15:22.850 --> 00:15:24.310
You’re right.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:28.570
We have to be more honest.

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.570
No one knows the future, after all.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:36.470
We have to treasure these feelings now.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:38.960
Let’s make our chocolates!

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.990
Yes, let’s make the extraordinary…

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.420
chocolates!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:46.760
It’s no good!

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:50.510
Even on this day, the Sakurazuki sisters aren’t here!

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:53.960
I guess it really was my fault…

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:59.270
Speaking of chocolates, I already got mine from the Ichijou sisters.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.600
You really got some?!

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:06.600
Of course, I bet you’re wishing you requested them directly like me.

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.190
It looks like it’s going well.

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.990
Yes, very… AH!

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:16.870
Ouch.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:19.450
It didn’t go well at all.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:23.520
But that’s okay, at least we got out of the room.

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:24.790
Yes, I suppose.

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:38.160
This is the first time we’ve walked all the way to school.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:40.310
Yes, it’s good that we didn’t get lost.

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:43.240
I wonder if Nozomu-kun
will come out soon.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:45.810
I hope he’ll be happy
to receive our chocolate.

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:46.880
Yes.

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:50.980
What? You won’t go home yet?

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:55.130
Yes, I’m expecting to get a few more chocolates.

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:56.080
I have to retrieve them.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.580
Uh-huh.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:06.830
Nozomu-kun is here!

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.650
Let’s go, Yura-chan!

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.670
Nozomu-chan!

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.840
Kaoruko-chan? Sumireko-chan?

00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:15.500
I’m glad we made it.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.100
You headed home right away.

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:20.260
Here, these are our feelings.

00:17:24.470 --> 00:17:27.650
Ah, I see. Since we’ve been friends since childhood…

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.900
That’s not the case.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:30.690
We’re serious.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:34.570
We told you, these are our feelings.

00:17:37.010 --> 00:17:41.540
Kaoruko-chan and Sumireko-chan are giving them to me and not to Yuuya?

00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:42.870
This can’t be happening.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:47.770
The two of us decided that we would treasure these feelings now.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:52.790
So if you would be honest and accept these, we would be happy.

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:04.170
Nozomu-kun took them!

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:08.200
That means he accepts the feelings of the Ichijou sisters.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.730
So that means Nozomu-kun really does have feelings for the Ichijou sisters.

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:17.870
Kira-chan, I have this sharp feeling around here that hurts.

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:19.710
I’m also in pain.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:27.300
Why, even after we said we’d be all right if Nozomu-kun was in love with someone else.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:28.350
Why?

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:28.830
Yes.

00:18:29.310 --> 00:18:31.200
See you later, Nozomu-chan.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.340
Ah, now I’m kind of embarrassed!

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.240
Let’s go home, Kira-chan.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:39.500
I can’t go back.

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:42.650
I can’t go back like this!

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:45.770
I have to know
Nozomu-kun’s true feelings!

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:47.180
Kira-chan!

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:51.150
Nozomu-kun.

00:18:51.640 --> 00:18:54.550
Kira-chan and Yura-chan saw me!

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:57.360
They saw me taking the chocolates!

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.650
I really am the worst.

00:19:04.510 --> 00:19:05.780
Take these.

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:06.580
Accept them…

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:10.330
Please!

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:12.080
These are our feelings.

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:14.460
Please!

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:15.090
Nozomu-kun!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:19.410
The two of us truly are in love with you!

00:19:19.410 --> 00:19:22.220
These feelings of ours will not lose to the Ichijou sisters’!

00:19:23.270 --> 00:19:25.010
Um, Nozomu-kun?

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:34.520
Misses, I have come for you.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:41.950
Ah, that’s… the Sakurazuki-sans’ car!
They’ve come!

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:46.240
These girls will be transferring to their old Jowaku Middle School.

00:19:46.810 --> 00:19:47.700
Transfer?

00:19:48.150 --> 00:19:49.140
Huh?

00:19:50.490 --> 00:19:54.510
They will never have to see you again, Futami-san.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:58.070
Misses, please get inside.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.070
Yes…

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:32.710
Kira-chan and Yura-chan, transferring?

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:35.250
What the hell did he mean
by “transferring”?

00:20:36.090 --> 00:20:39.480
What did he mean by
“They’ll never have to see you again”?

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:43.420
I…

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:47.260
Nozomu! Hey, Nozomu!

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:50.270
Just what in the world happened?

00:20:52.180 --> 00:20:55.440
Why? Why did it have to turn out like this?

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:59.210
I hurt Kira-chan and Yura-chan that much.

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:08.030
I’m just… I’m just…

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:15.920
Since that day I returned to this town, I’ve been surrounded by twins.

00:21:15.920 --> 00:21:17.750
All of them fell in love with me.

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:22.270
That shouldn’t be possible. It shouldn’t be possible…

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:30.180
Why? Why did it turn out like this?

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.060
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.060
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:10.890 --> 00:23:11.990
This is Nozomu.

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:15.450
Because of me, Kira-chan and Yura-chan will transfer schools.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:16.950
I have to do something.

00:23:16.950 --> 00:23:19.580
But what can I possibly do?

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:20.960
I’m in a pinch.

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:24.030
Next Time – Spring is in the Near Future…
